Firebase ke naye version (v11) mein Realtime Database create karne aur use connect karne ka tarika bohot simple hai. Aap ye steps follow karein:

### Step 1: Firebase Console par Database Banayein
1.  [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/) par jayein aur apna project select karein.
2.  Left sidebar mein **Build** menu par click karein aur **Realtime Database** select karein.
3.  **Create Database** button par click karein.
4.  Database ki **Location** select karein (Belgium ya United States) aur Next karein.
5.  **Start in Test Mode** select karein (taki shuruat mein read/write permission mil sake) aur **Enable** kar dein.

### Step 2: Database Rules Set Karein (Zaroori)
Agar aap chahte hain ki app bina login ke testing ke liye chale, to **Rules** tab mein ja kar ye rules paste kar dein aur **Publish** kardein:
```json
{
  "rules": {
    ".read": "true",
    ".write": "true"
  }
}
```

### Step 3: Database URL Check Karein
Database banane ke baad upar ek URL dikhega (jaise `https://your-project-id.firebaseio.com/`). 
Ye URL aapki `firebaseConfig` ke `databaseURL` field mein hona chahiye.

---

### Step 4: Code mein Integration (Naye Version ke mutabiq)

Aapki app mein maine pehle hi naye Modular SDK (v11) ke hisab se setup kar diya hai. Aapko bas `mockFirebase.ts` mein apni config update karni hai. 

**Naye version mein database access karne ka sahi tarika ye hai:**

```typescript
import { initializeApp } from 'firebase/app';
import { getDatabase, ref, set, onValue } from 'firebase/database';

// 1. Config (Jo aapne provide ki hai)
const firebaseConfig = {
  apiKey: "AIzaSy...",
  authDomain: "earningafiaclub.firebaseapp.com",
  databaseURL: "https://earningafiaclub-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com", // Ye sahi hona chahiye
  projectId: "earningafiaclub",
  // ... baki fields
};

// 2. Initialize
const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);
const db = getDatabase(app);

// 3. Data Save Karna (Naya Tareeka)
const saveData = async (path, data) => {
  await set(ref(db, path), data);
};

// 4. Data Read Karna (Naya Tareeka)
onValue(ref(db, 'users/123'), (snapshot) => {
  const data = snapshot.val();
  console.log(data);
});
```

### Aapko kya check karna hai?
Aapne jo `databaseURL` di hai: `https://earningafiaclub-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com`, check karein ki aapke Firebase Console mein bhi **exactly yahi URL** show ho raha hai. Agar URL alag hoga, to `Service database is not available` ka error aayega.

Aapka current code ab up-to-date hai aur inhi standards par chal raha hai. Bas console par ja kar "Realtime Database" ko **Enable** karna na bhoolein.

